{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And they complained, etc., in the wilderness.</b> Meaning, that their complaint was about His bringing them by way of the wilderness, for it was known as the way of the land of Canaan that there was only this route, and this was their complaint — that He brought them by way of the wilderness. But the matter was from HaShem, for mighty and known reasons, while Israel thought that it was Moses who had contrived to bring them by this route for a known reason."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:28:31.567820147Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}